.TH RASPIBOARD 1 "November 2026" "Raspiboard" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
raspiboard \- play sound clips locally and into recording applications
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B raspiboard
.SH DESCRIPTION
Raspiboard is a desktop soundboard using PipeWire for local playback and
routing clips alongside a recording application's microphone input.
Sound options include volume, cropping, overlapping playback, and global
shortcuts managed by the desktop portal.
.PP
Run Raspiboard in a graphical desktop session with PipeWire and a session
manager running. File dialogs require a desktop portal backend. Global
shortcuts require a backend implementing the Global Shortcuts portal.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.raspiboard/settings.toml
Saved application settings.
.TP
.I ~/.raspiboard/categories/
Saved sound assignments and options. Original audio files remain in their
original locations.
.TP
.I ~/.raspiboard/instance.lock
Single-instance lock. Do not delete this file while the application is running.
